course: dictionary
lesson: 14744
title: Spotting promotional words
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Promotional is an adjective. It describes something made to advertise a product or service, to help it sell. «The shop gave out free promotional pens with every bag.» The word promotional tells you the pens are there to make you remember the shop and want to buy from it.
explain: Promotional can also be about a better job. «Mum was excited about her promotional prospects at work.» Here it means she has a good chance of moving up to a higher position. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits: is it about selling, jobs, or sport?
explain: In sport, promotional means moving up to a higher league. «The club's promotional hopes rose after three wins in a row.» If the sentence is about a football team, the sport clues tell you which meaning to use.
fact: Promotional is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a poster, a video or a prospect.
fact: «Promotional» means made or used to advertise something and help it sell.
fact: «Promotional» can also mean to do with getting a better job or a higher position.
fact: In sport, «promotional» means to do with moving up to a higher league.
fact: Spotting promotional content, like adverts, free samples and special offers, helps you be a smart shopper.
exercise: «The shop gave out free promotional pens.» What does promotional mean here? | Used only inside the school | *Made to advertise and help the shop sell things | Made of plastic and very cheap | Given back when you are finished
exercise: Mum says she has good promotional prospects at work. What does promotional suggest? | A TV advert for cleaning products | *A chance of a better job or higher position | A free sample of food | A holiday abroad
exercise: Find and copy one word that means made to advertise: «The bakery handed out promotional cookies to passers-by.» | *promotional | handed | passers-by | bakery
test: «The band went on a promotional tour before their new album.» What is a promotional tour for? | To visit family far away | To train for a sports match | To clean the stage | *To advertise the band and sell their music
test: Sam says the football club hopes for promotional success this season. What does it mean? | *To move up to a higher league | To change their team colours | To sell their old kit | To lose every game
exam: «The sweets came with a promotional offer: two packets for the price of one.» Why is this promotional? | It is a recipe for baking | *It is an advert to persuade you to buy | It is a warning about sugar | It is a rule for the school
